Example:

Word present = 1
Word absent = 0
9. Laplace Smoothing

Suppose a word never appears in one class.

Its estimated probability may become zero.

Multiplying by zero makes the entire class likelihood zero.

Laplace smoothing helps prevent this.

For a multinomial word model:

P(word∣class)=Count(word,class)+1TotalWords(class)+V\boxed{P(word\mid class)=\frac{Count(word,class)+1}{TotalWords(class)+V}}

Where:

VV = Vocabulary size
Remember

Laplace Smoothing = Helps avoid zero probabilities.

